From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:27:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11105/11171] [outer-loop] Dashboard names the GPUs a job
 actually holds (REQ-INFRA-6840)

Twice today a GGUF run was reported as 'GPU 1 only' because the session had
SET CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU=1. That variable selects a preferred device
and does not mask the others, and Qwen3.8-27B at n_ctx 98304 exceeds one
24 GB card, so llama.cpp split it: 10,542 MiB on GPU 0 and 11,364 MiB on
GPU 1. The first misreport was corrected by hand in bd08d8d071 and the prose
written afterwards did not stop the second, so this is a check rather than
another rule.

gpu_indices_for joins nvidia-smi's pid,gpu_uuid to index,uuid and returns what
the driver reports. gpu_span_label prints 'SPANS GPU 0,1' for a multi-card run,
which is outside the conductor-owns-GPU-0 allocation and so is named
differently rather than listed the same way. An unmatched UUID is dropped, not
guessed.

REQ-INFRA-6840 was referenced by the existing dashboard test and had no spec
entry. Written down here rather than renumbered.

Rejected: parsing CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES or the launch environment. That is the
recalled state this requirement exists to forbid, and it is what produced both
misreports.

8 tests, 3/3 mutations RED on their named tests with byte-identical restores.
Verified firing live: the running r11l eval prints SPANS GPU 0,1.

